From aca013f3d5d562de045849b3f57e6162d6c24b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Alfuth <luke.alfuth@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] core: fix rules-correctness bugs in suit powers, plays,
 and the Jester

Suit powers were ordered with a comparator returning Equal for most pairs
but ordering Hearts vs Diamonds. That is not a total order, so a four-suit
combo could resolve Diamonds before Hearts and draw from a deck it had not
healed into yet. Newer toolchains can also panic on it outright.

Duplicate hand indices were accepted. Each remove shifts the hand, so a
repeated index pulled out a *different* card, letting a client play or
discard cards it never selected. Indices are validated up front now, so a
rejected selection also never disturbs the hand.

Spending the last solo Jester during the discard step and still coming up
short left the game parked in AwaitingDiscard: no legal move, no loss.

The Jester only offered the next-player choice at tables of three or more.
The rules say its player chooses *any* player to go next, and "any"
includes themselves, so two players is still a real choice: keep the turn
or pass it. The Jester is also played to the table rather than straight to
the discard pile, so a Hearts heal can no longer recycle it mid-fight.

Retroactive Jester powers are restricted to Spades. Hearts and Diamonds
are one-shot effects that already resolved, and Clubs is explicitly not
retroactive.

Yielding is refused once every other player has yielded on their last turn.

RULES_VERSION goes to 3, since play outcomes change.

test_diamond_draw_order never pinned active_enemy, so about one run in four
drew the immune Jack of Diamonds and failed on the draw it asserts.
